nes. Real wear and imperfections: scuffed floor, creased paper, dust in the light, fingerprints on glass. People appear only from behind, from the side with the face out of frame, or as hands. No readable text, letters, numbers, logos or brand names anywhere.", "negative_prompt": "faces, close-up of a face, text, letters, words, numbers, logos, watermark, brand names, CGI look, plastic skin, oversaturated, HDR, perfect symmetry, warped lines, extra fingers, distorted hands, floating objects, duplicated items, stock-photo smile, staged pose, lens flare, neon", "placeholders": null, "use_for": "Segment carousel, LinkedIn", "when_to_use": "Posts for manufacturers.", "fits_posts": "EDU-12", "text_space": "Top third", "on_image_text": "Materials in. Finished goods out."}, {"code": "PI-41", "kind": "post_image", "status": "to_generate", "title": "Spare parts shelving", "collection": "Segments", "pillar": "Visibility", "aspect": "4:5 · 1:1", "story": "Thousands of small parts in bins.", "prompt": "SHOT: Close view of shelving filled with plastic bins of small spare parts (filters, belts, bearings), a hand pulling one bin out, the rest softly out of focus. Aspect ratio 4:5.\n\nSETTING: A mid-size trading company's warehouse in an industrial area just outside Beirut, Lebanon: smooth grey concrete floor with faded yellow lane markings, tall blue-and-orange steel pallet racking, plain brown cartons and shrink-wrapped pallets of imported goods (lighting, small electronics, household items), a roll-up steel door letting in daylight, fluorescent tube lights, a small glass-walled office in one corner. Busy and real, not staged.\n\nPHOTO: A real close-up photograph taken on a full-frame camera with a 50mm lens at f/2, natural available light, true-to-life colours, fine film grain, shallow depth of field. Real texture: skin creases on hands, paper fibres, small scratches. No readable text, letters, numbers, logos or brand names anywhere; faces out of frame.", "negative_prompt": "faces, close-up of a face, text, letters, words, numbers, logos, watermark, brand names, CGI look, plastic skin, oversaturated, HDR, perfect symmetry, warped lines, extra fingers, distorted hands, floating objects, duplicated items, stock-photo smile, staged pose, lens flare, neon", "placeholders": null, "use_for": "Segment carousel", "when_to_use": "Importers and spare-parts dealers.", "fits_posts": "EDU-11, EDU-09", "text_space": "Top third", "on_image_text": "10,000 SKUs. Which bin?"}, {"code": "PI-42", "kind": "post_image", "status": "to_generate", "title": "Shop stockroom", "collection": "Segments", "pillar": "Visibility", "aspect": "4:5 · 9:16", "story": "The stockroom behind a retail branch.", "prompt": "SHOT: A narrow stockroom behind a shop: shelves of boxed products up to the ceiling, a half-open door showing the shop floor, a staff member's back as she reaches for a box. Aspect ratio 4:5.\n\nSETTING: Lebanon. Real places, real weather, real light; nothing polished or postcard-like.\n\nPHOTO: A real documentary-style photograph taken on a full-frame camera with a 35mm lens at f/2.8, natural available light, true-to-life slightly muted colours, fine film grain, gentle vignetting, straight vertical lines. Real wear and imperfections: scuffed floor, creased paper, dust in the light, fingerprints on glass. People appear only from behind, from the side with the face out of frame, or as hands. No readable text, letters, numbers, logos or brand names anywhere.", "negative_prompt": "faces, close-up of a face, text, letters, words, numbers, logos, watermark, brand names, CGI look, plastic skin, oversaturated, HDR, perfect symmetry, warped lines, extra fingers, distorted hands, floating objects, duplicated items, stock-photo smile, staged pose, lens flare, neon", "placeholders": null, "use_for": "Segment carousel (multi-branch retail)", "when_to_use": "Which branch has the last 12 units?", "fits_posts": "EDU-10", "text_space": "Top third", "on_image_text": "Which branch has the last 12?"}, {"code": "PI-43", "kind": "post_image", "status": "to_generate", "title": "Dot cube hero", "collection": "Brand graphics", "pillar": "Brand", "aspect": "1:1 · 4:5 · 9:16", "story": "A glowing cube made of dots — the Stacko idea in one image.", "prompt": "SHOT: A glowing isometric cube made of small luminous dots, three faces in three shades of teal and blue, a bright white glowing core where three thin gaps meet, floating above a dark reflective surface. Aspect ratio 1:1.\n\nRENDER: A clean, minimal 3D render on a deep navy background (#0E2440) with a soft radial glow of #1B416B, glowing teal (#0895A6) and cyan (#2EF2EE) accents, soft studio light, isometric view, premium and calm. No text, letters or logos.", "negative_prompt": "text, letters, logos, watermark, clutter, harsh shadows, photorealistic people", "placeholders": null, "use_for": "Carousel covers, 'Meet Stacko', announcements", "when_to_use": "Brand-level posts. Put the real logo on top, never an AI one.", "fits_posts": "NOV-03, EDU-72", "text_space": "Around the cube", "on_image_text": "Your stock, always in sight."}, {"code": "PI-44", "kind": "post_image", "status": "to_generate", "title": "Warehouses on a map (concept)", "collection": "Brand graphics", "pillar": "Visibility", "aspect": "1:1 · 4:5", "story": "Three small warehouses connected by glowing routes.", "prompt": "SHOT: Three small isometric warehouse buildings on a dark stylised map, connected by thin glowing teal route lines, a tiny truck on one route, a small ship icon on a dashed sea route. Aspect ratio 1:1.\n\nRENDER: A clean, minimal 3D render on a deep navy background (#0E2440) with a soft radial glow of #1B416B, glowing teal (#0895A6) and cyan (#2EF2EE) accents, soft studio light, isometric view, premium and calm. No text, letters or logos.", "negative_prompt": "text, letters, logos, watermark, clutter, harsh shadows, photorealistic people", "placeholders": null, "use_for": "Concept carousel cover, explainer slide", "when_to_use": "When explaining the map idea in a simple, illustrated way.", "fits_posts": "NOV-12, D30-20, EDU-45", "text_space": "Top third", "on_image_text": "From scattered to one map."}]$lib$::jsonb) as i(code text, kind text, status text, title text, collection text,
    pillar text, aspect text, reference text, prompt text, negative_prompt text, placeholders text, use_for text,
    when_to_use text, fits_posts text, story text, text_space text, on_image_text text, notes text)
  on conflict (brand_id, code) do nothing;

  -- Files already stored for a code with no entry (added to the kit after the sheets).
  insert into public.library_items (brand_id, code, kind, status, title, collection, aspect, placeholders, use_for, when_to_use)
  select distinct on (a.metadata ->> 'code') v_brand, a.metadata ->> 'code', a.asset_type::text, 'generated',
    coalesce(a.metadata ->> 'shot', a.metadata ->> 'image', a.metadata ->> 'code'), a.metadata ->> 'set',
    a.metadata ->> 'aspect', a.metadata ->> 'screens', a.metadata ->> 'use_for', a.metadata ->> 'when'
  from public.brand_assets a
  where a.brand_id = v_brand and a.asset_type::text in ('background', 'graphic', 'post_image')
    and a.metadata ->> 'code' ~ '^(BG|GFX|PI)-[0-9]{2,3}$'
  order by a.metadata ->> 'code', a.version desc
  on conflict (brand_id, code) do nothing;

  -- A stored file means the image exists.
  update public.library_items i set status = 'generated'
  where i.brand_id = v_brand and i.status = 'to_generate'
    and exists (select 1 from public.brand_assets a where a.brand_id = v_brand and a.metadata ->> 'code' = i.code);
end $$;
